Gradient descent is an optimization algorithm used to minimize a function by iteratively moving in the direction of the steepest decrease of the function. It starts at an initial point and updates the parameters using the negative gradient of the function.

What is the difference between gradient descent and stochastic gradient descent?

Gradient descent uses the entire dataset to compute the gradient at each step, which can be computationally expensive for large datasets. Stochastic gradient descent (SGD) updates the parameters using only a single data point at each step, making it faster but noisier. Mini-batch gradient descent is a compromise, using a small subset of
